---
import LegalLayout from "../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — CG Design & Co."
  description="How CG Design & Co. collects, uses, shares and protects your personal data, and your rights in Australia, the UK and the EU."
  pageTitle="Privacy Policy"
  lastUpdated="20 November 2026"
>
  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    This website is run by CG Design &amp; Co., a registered business name
    (ABN 25 672 082 550) based at St Luke Street, Randwick NSW 2031,
    Australia ("we", "us", "our"). We decide how your personal data is
    used, which makes us the "controller" of it under UK and EU data
    protection law.
  </p>
  <p>
    For anything in this policy, including a request about your data, email
    <a href="mailto:info@cgdesignaus.com">info@cgdesignaus.com</a> or write
    to us at the address above.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Enquiries</strong> — when you use the contact form: your name,
      email address, business name, website or social link (if you give
      one), and what you're interested in (including anything you picked in
      the quote builder).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Messages</strong> — anything you send us by email or WhatsApp,
      including your phone number if you message us on WhatsApp.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Client details</strong> — if you hire us: your contact and
      billing details, the content you send for your website (text, photos,
      logos), and any account logins you choose to share so we can set things
      up for you.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Payments</strong> — handled by Stripe. We see the amount, date
      and the name and email on the payment, but never your full card
      details.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Technical data</strong> — your IP address, browser and device
      type, which your browser sends to any website it loads. On the contact
      page, our spam protection (hCaptcha) also looks at how the page is used,
      such as mouse and keyboard activity, to tell people from bots.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We don't use analytics, advertising or tracking tools on this site, and
    we never sell your data or share it for anyone else's marketing.
  </p>

  <h2>Why we use it, and our legal basis</h2>
  <p>
    UK and EU law asks us to name a legal basis for each use. Australian law
    asks us to use your data only for the purpose you gave it for, or a
    related one you'd reasonably expect.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Replying to your enquiry and preparing a quote</strong> —
      because you asked us to (steps before a contract), and our legitimate
      interest in answering people who contact us.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Doing the work you've hired us for, invoicing and support</strong>
      — to carry out our contract with you.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Keeping tax and accounting records</strong> — because the law
      requires it.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Stopping spam and keeping the site secure</strong> — our
      legitimate interest in protecting the site and our inbox.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We'll only send you marketing emails if you've asked for them, and you
    can stop them at any time. We don't make decisions about you using
    automated profiling.
  </p>

  <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>
    We use a small number of service providers who handle data on our
    behalf, only for the purpose described:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Web3Forms</strong> — delivers contact form submissions to our
      inbox.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>hCaptcha</strong> (Intuition Machines, Inc., USA) — spam
      protection on the contact form. See
      <a href="https://www.hcaptcha.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">hCaptcha's privacy policy</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Stripe</strong> — takes payments. See
      <a href="https://stripe.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Stripe's privacy policy</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>GitHub Pages</strong> (GitHub, Inc., USA) — hosts this website
      and keeps short-term server logs, including IP addresses, for security.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Our email provider</strong> — stores the emails we send and
      receive.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>WhatsApp</strong> (Meta) — only if you choose to message us
      there.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We may also share data if the law requires it, or with professional
    advisers such as an accountant, under a duty of confidentiality.
  </p>

  <h2>International transfers</h2>
  <p>
    We're based in Australia, and some of our service providers are in the
    United States and other countries. If you contact us from the UK or the
    EU, your data will be handled outside the UK and the European Economic
    Area.
  </p>
  <p>
    Australia doesn't have a UK or EU "adequacy" decision. When you send us
    an enquiry or hire us, the transfer to us in Australia is necessary to
    reply to you and to carry out what you've asked for. For our service
    providers, we rely on the safeguards they offer, such as the UK
    International Data Transfer Addendum or the EU Standard Contractual
    Clauses, or the UK–US Data Bridge where a provider is certified. Ask us
    if you'd like more detail.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Enquiries that don't go ahead</strong> — up to 2 years after
      we last heard from you, then deleted.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Client records and invoices</strong> — up to 7 years after the
      end of our work together, because tax and accounting law requires us
      to keep records.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Logins you share with us</strong> — deleted when the job they
      were for is finished, or straight away if you ask.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Keeping it safe</h2>
  <p>
    We keep your data in password-protected accounts and only use it for
    the job it was given for. No method of sending or storing data is perfectly secure, but if
    something ever went wrong that put you at risk, we'd tell you and the
    relevant regulator as the law requires.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>Wherever you live, you can ask us to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Tell you what personal data we hold about you and give you a copy.</li>
    <li>Correct anything that's wrong or out of date.</li>
    <li>Delete your data, unless we must keep it by law.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>If you're in the UK or the EU, you also have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Restrict how we use your data while a concern is looked into.</li>
    <li>Object to us using your data on the basis of our legitimate interests.</li>
    <li>Receive the data you gave us in a common, machine-readable format, or have it sent to someone else.</li>
    <li>Withdraw your consent at any time, where we rely on it.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Email <a href="mailto:info@cgdesignaus.com">info@cgdesignaus.com</a> to
    make a request. It's free, and we'll reply within one month. We may need
    to confirm who you are first.
  </p>

  <h2>Complaints</h2>
  <p>
    Please tell us first and we'll try to put it right. You can also
    complain to a regulator:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Australia</strong> — the
      <a href="https://www.oaic.gov.au/privacy/privacy-complaints" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Office of the Australian Information Commissioner (OAIC)</a>,
      1300 363 992.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>United Kingdom</strong> — the
      <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Information Commissioner's Office (ICO)</a>,
      0303 123 1113.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>European Union</strong> — the data protection authority in the
      country where you live or work.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    This site doesn't use tracking or advertising cookies. See our
    <a href={`${base}/cookies-policy/`}>Cookies Policy</a> for the little it
    does store.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    Our services are for adults and businesses. We don't knowingly collect
    data from anyone under 16.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We'll update this policy when the way we handle data changes. The date
    at the top shows when it last changed.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
